Actually, I've got a solution to this problem of mine: the "Pick a
role" menu is always followed by another menu - and the name of that
menu mentions the role you just chose - for example, "Pick the race of
your Archeologist".

Here's the idea: each menu displays an ASCII picture of the selection
made in the previous menu. For "Pick the alignment of your female human
Archeologist" there'd be a picture of a female human Archeologist. For
"Pick the gender of your human Archeologist" there'd either be a
picture of a female human Archeologist, or a picture of a male human
Archeologist. For "Pick the race of your Archeologist" there'd be a
picture of an Archeologist of random race and gender. (But "Pick a
role" would still have no picture.)

However... the dimensions of the pictures will be limited by the width
of the largest menu these pictures will complement. This is complicated
by the fact that some menus (like the alignment menu) are skipped for
races or classes with fixed alignment/race/gender choices. Thus, the
widest menu encountered by the picture of a female human Wizard is the
one entitled "Pick the alignment of your female human Wizard" (46
chars) whereas the widest menu encountered by the picture of a female
elven Wizard is the one entitled "Pick the gender of your elven Wizard"
(36 chars) as elven Wizards are always chaotic aligned.

